## Instructions for Customizing This Template

### 1. Replace Placeholders

- `{{PACKAGE}}`: Screen package (e.g., `com.greenrobotdev.linklibrary.screens.home`)
- `{{FEATURE_NAME}}`: Feature name (e.g., "Home", "Link Detail")
- `{{STATE_CLASS_NAME}}`: State class (e.g., `HomeState`)
- `{{EVENT_CLASS_NAME}}`: Event interface (e.g., `HomeEvent`)
- `{{USECASE_FUNCTION_NAME}}`: Function name (e.g., `HomeUseCase`)
- `{{REPOSITORY_PACKAGE}}`: Repository package
- `{{REPOSITORY_NAME}}`: Repository variable name (e.g., `linkRepository`)
- `{{REPOSITORY_TYPE}}`: Repository type (e.g., `LinkRepository`)

### 2. Define State Variables

Create a mutable state variable for each state property:

```kotlin
var isLoading by remember { mutableStateOf(initialState.isLoading) }
var error by remember { mutableStateOf(initialState.error) }
var links by remember { mutableStateOf(initialState.links) }
var searchQuery by remember { mutableStateOf(initialState.searchQuery) }
```

### 3. Implement Initial Data Loading

Use `LaunchedEffect(Unit)` for one-time setup:

```kotlin
LaunchedEffect(Unit) {
    isLoading = true
    linkRepository.getLinks().collect { result ->
        isLoading = false
        result.onSuccess { entities ->
            links = entities.map { it.toDomain() }
                .sortedByDescending { it.createdAt }
                .take(20)
        }
        result.onFailure { error = it.message }
    }
}
```

